20. Senior-Level Design Question
Interviewer

When would you choose Karpenter over Cluster Autoscaler?

Strong Answer

"I prefer Karpenter in EKS environments where workloads are dynamic and require multiple instance types. It provides faster provisioning, better packing efficiency, support for Spot capacity, and removes the need to manage many Auto Scaling Groups.

For legacy environments already heavily invested in managed node groups and Cluster Autoscaler, migration may not always be immediately necessary.

For new EKS platforms, Karpenter is generally my preferred node autoscaling solution."

